  "strategy": "U/B Heartless Emerge Tempo",
  "colors": "UB",
  "identity": "A two-colour tempo deck that treats its own creatures as mana. Every mid-curve body it plays is priced as future fuel: emerge reduces an Eldrazi's cost by the sacrificed creature's mana value, so a Mist Raven or Tower Geist that already bounced a blocker or drew a card converts on turn four or five into a 5/6 that taps the opponent's board, a 6/4 that drains three, or a 3/4 flier that replaces itself. Heartless Summoning accelerates both halves at once, cutting {2} from the fodder on the way down and {2} from the Eldrazi on the way up. The deck wins by never trading down — the sacrifice is a cost already paid, so the bodies it loses are bodies it had finished using.",
